| !Run for !Warzone2100 - RISC OS port of Warzone 2100 2.3.9
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked with
| riscos-mesa (software OpenGL) and its SDL2, and converted to an Absolute
| (AIF) file, so !SharedLibs isn't needed.

Set Warzone2100$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <Warzone2100$Dir>.!Sprites

| --- Runtime support -------------------------------------------------
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error Warzone 2100 needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error Warzone 2100 needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
| PThreadTicker (from riscos-unixlib) runs UnixLib's thread switcher, so it
| is always paged in, whichever task is. A copy in !System is used if it's
| newer; without the module the game runs the same code from the RMA.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <Warzone2100$Dir>.PThrTicker

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager and SharedSound
| (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound. SharedSoundBuffer and
| StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without
| them the game plays silently. Volume: Options > Sound in the game.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| --- Files ------------------------------------------------------------
| Paths handed to the program are UnixLib paths of the form /<Var$Dir>/...
| Set and Do expand <variables>, so they are written /|<Var$Dir>/... here:
| "|<" keeps the "<", and UnixLib expands the variable when it's used.
| Settings, saved games and screenshots go in Choices.
CDir <Choices$Write>.Warzone2100
| Fonts: the bundled DejaVu fonts, found through fontconfig.
Set FONTCONFIG_FILE /|<Warzone2100$Dir>/fonts/fonts.conf
CDir <Wimp$ScrapDir>.WZ2100fc

| --- Memory ---------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap goes in a dynamic area, "Warzone2100 Heap" (up to 512MB,
| removed when the game quits), so the WimpSlot only has to hold the
| program itself (about 25MB).
WimpSlot -min 32768K -max 32768K

| --- Display ---------------------------------------------------------
| The game opens a 1024x768 desktop window (smaller on small screens)
| unless the Choices say otherwise (Options > Video in the game). Everything is drawn by software OpenGL, so
| bigger windows and full screen are slower.
| Uncomment one of these to force a mode from here instead:
| Set Warzone2100$Mode --window --resolution 800x600
| Set Warzone2100$Mode --fullscreen --resolution 640x480
If "<Warzone2100$Mode>"="" Then Set Warzone2100$Mode --window

| --- Texture filtering ----------------------------------------------
| Software OpenGL: filtering is most of the cost of drawing the ground.
| fast (the default): bilinear; nearest: fastest, blocky close up;
| smooth: trilinear; best: trilinear + anisotropic (as on other systems).
| Set Warzone2100$Filter to one of those before running the game (or
| uncomment the line below); the game saves the choice in its Choices.
| Set Warzone2100$Filter nearest
Unset Warzone2100$FilterArg
If "<Warzone2100$Filter>"<>"" Then Set Warzone2100$FilterArg --texfilter=<Warzone2100$Filter>

| --- Logging --------------------------------------------------------
| Errors always go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.Warzone2100log (empty after a normal
| run), so a game that fails to start leaves a message and any crash
| backtrace there. For a full log, set Warzone2100$Log (remove the | from
| the next line, or *Set Warzone2100$Log 1 before running the game): the
| game's own log then goes to <Choices$Write>.Warzone2100.WZlog as well.
| Set Warzone2100$Log 1
Set Warzone2100$Output /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/Warzone2100log
Unset Warzone2100$LogArg
If "<Warzone2100$Log>"<>"" Then Set Warzone2100$LogArg --debugfile=/|<Choices$Write>/Warzone2100/WZlog
| With logging on, UnixLib also adds a line of thread switcher counters to
| <Wimp$ScrapDir>.WZTickerStats when the game quits. (The variable is
| read by every UnixLib program; *Unset UnixLib$TickerStats to stop.)
If "<Warzone2100$Log>"<>"" Then Set UnixLib$TickerStats <Wimp$ScrapDir>.WZTickerStats
| For a more detailed log (with Warzone2100$Log set), also set e.g.
|   *Set Warzone2100$Debug --debug=all --flush-debug-stderr
| (the log gets big quickly; *Unset Warzone2100$Debug afterwards).

| --- Program -------------------------------------------------------
Do Run <Warzone2100$Dir>.warzone2100 --datadir=/|<Warzone2100$Dir>/data --configdir=/|<Choices$Write>/Warzone2100 <Warzone2100$Mode> <Warzone2100$FilterArg> <Warzone2100$LogArg> <Warzone2100$Debug> %*0
